# Every licence a package in this tree may be under, and why each one is here.
#
# licence-scan reads this file and nothing else does. An entry is one line
# holding one SPDX licence identifier, or `package <name>` for a dependency that
# declares no licence at all and is taken anyway. The line immediately above an
# entry is its reason, and licence-scan refuses an entry that has none, so a
# licence cannot join this list without somebody writing down why it may.
#
# THE QUESTION EVERY REASON ANSWERS is whether this project can be distributed
# as a whole under its own licence with that package inside it. It is not
# whether the licence is well known, and it is not whether the package is
# popular. A permissive licence is here because its terms are carried forward by
# a stronger one; a copyleft licence is here only where it is the same one this
# project already uses.
#
# THESE ARE JUDGEMENTS AND NOT LEGAL ADVICE. What is checkable is that the
# question was asked and the answer was written down. docs/licence.md is where
# the same position is stated in prose for an operator, and the residual is
# stated there rather than hidden here: a declaration in a package's own
# metadata is what this list is compared against, and nobody in this tree has
# read the licence text of any dependency.
#
# THE LIST HOLDS WHAT THE TREE ACTUALLY CARRIES. A licence added before a
# package needs it is a decision made without a case in front of it, and it sits
# here afterwards looking like one somebody made deliberately.

# The project's own licence, which every workspace member declares and which the
# two manifests have to agree on before licence-scan will judge anything.
AGPL-3.0-only

# Permissive, with no condition beyond attribution and the notice, so the
# combined work carries this project's licence and the notice travels with it.
MIT

# Permissive, and its patent and notice terms are additional permissions and
# requirements that version 3 of this project's licence is written to carry.
# Version 2 is not, which is why the version this project uses is not incidental.
Apache-2.0

# A dedication to the public domain with a permissive fallback, so it imposes
# nothing on the combined work. Reached here as one half of an OR with MIT.
Unlicense

# Permissive, covering the Unicode character data one dependency compiles in.
# It reaches this tree as the AND half of "(MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Unicode-3.0",
# which is what makes it a separate decision rather than one the OR absorbs.
Unicode-3.0
